TITLE:: SPRouting
summary:: the node tree read as a signal flow: who writes and reads each bus, in the server's order
categories:: Libraries>ServerPanel
related:: Classes/SPTree, Classes/SPProbe, Classes/SynthDesc, Classes/In, Classes/InFeedback

DESCRIPTION::
From each synth's SynthDef (its code::In:: and code::Out:: UGens) and its control values, a model of the busses: for every bus channel the synths that write it and those that read it, in the order the server runs them. Language only: nothing here touches the server. link::Classes/SPTree:: builds one at every answer of the server and shows it as its busses view, its problems, and the path of a signal.

The order rule it checks is the server's: code::In.ar:: hears a bus only if a synth earlier in the tree wrote it in the same block. A reader placed before its source hears silence; code::InFeedback:: hears the block before, wherever it is.

What it can not know: a synth whose SynthDef this sclang has no link::Classes/SynthDesc:: of (the model's code::unknown:: counts them), a bus worked out inside the graph, a bus a control is mapped to.

code::
(
SynthDef(\rt_src, { |out = 20| Out.ar(out, SinOsc.ar(300) * 0.1) }).add;
SynthDef(\rt_fx, { |in = 20, out = 22| Out.ar(out, In.ar(in) * 0.5) }).add;
// a tree as SPTree parses it: the effect before its source
t = (id: 0, kind: \group, children: [
	(id: 1001, kind: \synth, def: \rt_fx, controls: [[\in, 20], [\out, 22]]),
	(id: 1002, kind: \synth, def: \rt_src, controls: [[\out, 20]])
]);
m = SPRouting.build(Server.default, t);
SPRouting.problems(m).do { |p| p[\text].postln };
SPRouting.ranges(m).do { |r| [r[\rate], r[\index], r[\w], r[\r]].postln };
);
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: build
The model of a tree.
ARGUMENT:: server
The link::Classes/Server:: (for which busses are hardware).
ARGUMENT:: tree
A node Event: code::id::, code::kind:: (code::\group:: or code::\synth::), code::children:: for a group, code::def:: and code::controls:: (code::[name, value]:: pairs) for a synth.
ARGUMENT:: controlsOf
A function of a synth's id answering its controls, for a node that has none.
RETURNS:: an link::Classes/Event::: code::order:: (the synths, in the server's order), code::nodes:: and code::pos:: (by id), code::ios:: (each synth's busses), code::audio:: and code::control:: (per bus channel: code::writers:: and code::readers::, each code::(id:, type:)::), code::unknown::

METHOD:: iosOf
A synth's busses with their numbers.
ARGUMENT:: def
Its SynthDef's name.
ARGUMENT:: controls
Its controls, code::[name, value]:: pairs; the def's defaults stand in for what is missing.
RETURNS:: an Array of Events code::(dir:, rate:, channels:, type:, bus:, via:)::, code::bus:: nil when it is not a plain number; nil without a SynthDesc

METHOD:: templateOf
A def's In and Out UGens, before any control value: code::start:: is a bus number, a control's name, or nil.
ARGUMENT:: def
A SynthDef's name.

METHOD:: controlDict
A synth's control values by name: the def's defaults, then what the server said.
ARGUMENT:: def
A SynthDef's name.
ARGUMENT:: controls
code::[name, value]:: pairs.

METHOD:: buffersOf
The buffers a synth's controls name: a control whose name says code::buf:: and whose value is a whole number.
ARGUMENT:: def
A SynthDef's name.
ARGUMENT:: controls
code::[name, value]:: pairs.
RETURNS:: code::[[control, bufnum] ...]::

METHOD:: ranges
The busses as rows: neighbouring channels with the same writers and readers are one row.
ARGUMENT:: model
From link::#*build::.
RETURNS:: an Array of Events code::(rate:, index:, channels:, kind:, writers:, readers:, w:, r:, name:)::, code::w:: and code::r:: the ids

METHOD:: busKind
code::\out:: (a hardware output), code::\in:: (a hardware input), code::\private:: or code::\control::.
ARGUMENT:: server
The link::Classes/Server::.
ARGUMENT:: rate
code::\audio:: or code::\control::.
ARGUMENT:: index
The bus index.

METHOD:: problems
What looks wrong in the order. A reader is early when a new source of its bus runs after it: a synth that writes the bus and is not itself downstream of it (link::#*downstreamOf::). It is a warning when nothing writes the bus before the reader, now or ever while code::fed:: was kept; else a note. A bus with only one end is a note.
ARGUMENT:: model
From link::#*build::.
ARGUMENT:: fed
A link::Classes/Set:: the caller keeps between calls: which readers have ever had a writer before them.
RETURNS:: an Array of Events code::(level:, kind:, id:, bus:, text:, key:)::

METHOD:: downstreamOf
The synths that are downstream of a bus channel: those that read it, and those that read what such a synth wrote. What they write back to the bus is the bus itself, processed - a mixer's send, effect, return and fader on one bus - not a new source.
ARGUMENT:: model
From link::#*build::.
ARGUMENT:: index
An audio bus channel.
RETURNS:: an link::Classes/IdentitySet:: of node ids

METHOD:: pathFrom
Where a signal goes: from a synth, or a bus, through every reader that hears it, to the hardware outputs.
ARGUMENT:: model
From link::#*build::.
ARGUMENT:: start
code::(kind: \synth, id:):: or code::(kind: \bus, rate:, index:, channels:)::.
ARGUMENT:: levels
A function of a bus channel answering its level, or nil when nothing is measured.
ARGUMENT:: paused
The ids of the paused synths.
RETURNS:: code::(rows:, verdicts:, truncated:)::. A row is a step: code::\synth::, code::\bus:: (with its level) or code::\note::, with its depth. A verdict is code::(ok:, text:)::: that it reaches an output, or the first place the sound stops

METHOD:: feedsOf
Who feeds a synth: for each bus it reads, the synths that write it where it can hear them.
ARGUMENT:: model
From link::#*build::.
ARGUMENT:: id
A synth's node id.

METHOD:: busText
A bus in words: code::"audio 16-17 (orbit 0 dry)"::.
ARGUMENT:: server
The link::Classes/Server::.
ARGUMENT:: rate
code::\audio:: or code::\control::.
ARGUMENT:: index
The first channel.
ARGUMENT:: channels
How many.
ARGUMENT:: name
Its name, when already known.

METHOD:: nodeText
A node in words: code::"nt_src (1004)"::.
ARGUMENT:: model
From link::#*build::.
ARGUMENT:: id
A node id.

METHOD:: whoText
Several nodes in words: one of a kind with its id, more as code::"nt_blip ×3"::.
ARGUMENT:: model
From link::#*build::.
ARGUMENT:: ids
Node ids.

METHOD:: silence
The amplitude under which a bus is silent: 0.0001 (-80 dB).
